Z||000003||owenslee||04-11-2001||05:36 PM||||For those interested in buying the June and July 1994 back issues of Automotive Rebuilder...they MAY be available.<P>You would need to call 312-762-2193 or fax 708-656-1990 attn: subscription dept.<P>Back issues are shown as available for $5.95 ea. for domestic delivery, but I have not called to confirm.<P>Kerry<P>------------------<BR>"Badges?...Badges..??? We don gat to sho yu no stinkin' BADGES..!!!"<p>[This message has been edited by owenslee (edited 04-12-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000004||rockcrawl||04-15-2001||08:16 PM||||I finally got to reading all those pages. I'll print them and store them for later reference. I'm pretty sure nobody will want to rebuild one of those engines after reading that! My '90 4.5PFI is a one-year-wonder just like I suspected. I was too scared to remove the boreliners from my engine, I just left them in place and honed them. One thing has me worried though, they say the intake gasket with the resticted coolant port goes on the right head. Well I didn't notice any difference between the two gaskets and the Chilton's book doesn't say anything about it. The gasket set is showing qty 2 of the same # for the gaskets, so I guess they are both the same. I hope so because it's too late now. Anyway, thanks for posting that info. I won't be tackling any full rebuilds, but it helps to identify the different engines and explains the differences. And for anyone considering one of these engines, be prepared to spend about $200 just for the full gasket set.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
